1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:06,901
In formal English you can drop if and move the auxiliary in front of the subject, in three patterns only.

2
00:00:06,901 --> 00:00:09,127
If I were you: were I you.

3
00:00:09,127 --> 00:00:11,549
If he had told me: had he told me.

4
00:00:11,549 --> 00:00:14,075
If you should need help: should you need help.

5
00:00:14,075 --> 00:00:18,919
And once if is gone, it must not come back: never if had I known.

